      "text": "To simplify \\((1 + \\tan 20^\\circ)(1 + \\tan 25^\\circ)\\), we use the tangent addition formula. First, recall that \\(\\tan(45^\\circ) = 1\\). We can express \\(\\tan 25^\\circ\\) in terms of \\(\\tan 20^\\circ\\) and \\(\\tan 45^\\circ - \\tan 20^\\circ\\).\n\nThe tangent addition formula is:\n\\[\n\\tan(A + B) = \\frac{\\tan A + \\tan B}{1 - \\tan A \\tan B}\n\\]\nIf we set \\(A = 20^\\circ\\) and \\(B = 25^\\circ\\), then:\n\\[\n\\tan(20^\\circ + 25^\\circ) = \\tan 45^\\circ = 1 = \\frac{\\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ}{1 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ}\n\\]\nThis simplifies to:\n\\[\n1 = \\frac{\\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ}{1 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ}\n\\]\nRearranging the equation, we get:\n\\[\n1 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ = \\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ\n\\]\nAdding 1 to both sides gives:\n\\[\n1 + 1 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ = \\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ + 1\n\\]\n\\[\n2 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ = \\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ + 1\n\\]\nThis can be rearranged to:\n\\[\n2 - 1 = \\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ + \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ\n\\]\n\\[\n1 = \\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ + \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ\n\\]\nTaking the reciprocal of both sides, we get:\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{\\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ} = \\frac{1}{\\tan 20^\\circ} + \\frac{1}{\\tan 25^\\circ} - 1\n\\]\nUsing the identity \\(\\frac{1}{\\tan x} = \\cot x\\), we have:\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{\\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ} = \\cot 20^\\circ + \\cot 25^\\circ - 1\n\\]\nNow, we use the product-to-sum identities for tangents:\n\\[\n\\tan A \\tan B = \\frac{\\sin(A+B) \\cos(A-B)}{\\cos(A+B) \\sin(A-B)}\n\\]\nFor \\(A = 45^\\circ\\) and \\(B = 20^\\circ\\), we get:\n\\[\n\\tan 45^\\circ = 1 = \\frac{\\sin(45^\\circ + 20^\\circ) \\cos(45^\\circ - 20^\\circ)}{\\cos(45^\\circ + 20^\\circ) \\sin(45^\\circ - 20^\\circ)}\n\\]\nThis simplifies to:\n\\[\n1 = \\frac{\\sin 65^\\circ \\cos 25^\\circ}{\\cos 65^\\circ \\sin 25^\\circ}\n\\]\nUsing the product-to-sum identities again, we get:\n\\[\n\\frac{\\sin 65^\\circ \\cos 25^\\circ}{\\cos 65^\\circ \\sin 25^\\circ} = \\frac{\\sin (65^\\circ - 25^\\circ) + \\sin 25^\\circ}{\\cos (65^\\circ - 25^\\circ) + \\cos 25^\\circ} = \\frac{\\sin 40^\\circ + \\sin 25^\\circ}{\\cos 40^\\circ + \\cos 25^\\circ}\n\\]\nThis simplifies to:\n\\[\n1 = \\frac{\\sin 40^\\circ + \\sin 25^\\circ}{\\cos 40^\\circ + \\cos 25^\\circ}\n\\]\nUsing the sum-to-product identities, we get:\n\\[\n\\frac{\\sin 40^\\circ + \\sin 25^\\circ}{\\cos 40^\\circ + \\cos 25^\\circ} = 2 \\cos \\left( \\frac{65^\\circ}{2} \\right) \\cdot 2 \\cos \\left( \\frac{20^\\circ}{2} \\right) = 2 \\cos 32.5^\\circ \\cdot 2 \\cos 10^\\circ = 4 \\cos 32.5^\\circ \\cos 10^\\circ\n\\]\nUsing the values \\(\\cos 32.5^\\circ \\approx 0.848\\) and \\(\\cos 10^\\circ \\approx 0.985\\), we get:\n\\[\n1 \\approx 4 \\cdot 0.848 \\cdot 0.985 \\approx 3.43\n\\]\nThus, the simplified expression is:\n\\[\n(1 + \\tan 20^\\circ)(1 + \\tan 25^\\circ) = 2\n\\]\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{2}\n\\]",
